*{{flagicon|Belarus}} [[Brest, Belarus|Brest]] and [[Grodno]] — Visa not required for 10 days.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://eng.belta.by/president/view/visa-free-travel-time-up-to-ten-days-in-parts-of-brest-oblast-grodno-oblast-as-from-1-january-107990-2017/|title=Visa-free travel time up to ten days in parts of Brest Oblast, Grodno Oblast as from 1 January|date=26 December 2017}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Crimea}} [[Crimea]] — Visa issued by Russia is required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.themoscowtimes.com/news/article/foreigners-now-need-russian-visa-to-visit-crimea/497173.html|title=Foreigners Now Need Russian Visa to Visit Crimea|website=themoscowtimes.com|date=April 2014 |access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|Northern Cyprus}} — Visa free access for 3 months. Passport required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cypnet.co.uk/ncyprus/tourism/tourist.html |title=How to get to North Cyprus? - Passport, Visa & Entry Requirements |publisher=Cypnet.co.uk |access-date=25 July 2018}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|United Nations}} [[United Nations Buffer Zone in Cyprus|UN Buffer Zone in Cyprus]] — Access Permit is required for travelling inside the zone, except Civil Use Areas.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.unficyp.org/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=1608&tt=graphic&lang=l1 |title=UNFICYP > Buffer Zone Permits |access-date=1 August 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141021143210/http://www.unficyp.org/nqcontent.cfm?a_id=1608&tt=graphic&lang=l1 |archive-date=21 October 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|Gibraltar}} — Visa not required.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=CA|destination=GI|accessdate=26 November 2013}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Norway}} [[Jan Mayen]] — Permit issued by the local police required for staying for less than 24 hours<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.jan-mayen.no/visit.htm|title=Jan Mayen Homesite, Edited by the Jan Mayen Crew|website=www.jan-mayen.no|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-date=30 April 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130430074108/http://www.jan-mayen.no/visit.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref> and permit issued by the [[Norwegian Police Service|Norwegian police]] for staying for more than 24 hours.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.lovdata.no/for/sf/jd/xd-19620601-0001.html |title=Forskrifter om utlendingers adgang til Jan Mayen |language=no |trans-title=Regulations on foreigners' access to Jan Mayen |website=lovdata.no |access-date=7 March 2022 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220307005017/https://lovdata.no/dokument/SF/forskrift/1962-06-01-1 |archive-date=7 March 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>
*{{flag|Svalbard}} of {{flag|Norway}} — Right to live and work under the [[Svalbard Treaty]].
*{{flag|Kosovo}} — Visa free for 90 days.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mfa-ks.net/?page=2,158|title=Special Categories Exempted From Visa Requirements - For Foreign Citizens - Consular Services - Ministry of Foreign Affairs - Republic of Kosovo|website=Ministry of Foreign Affairs - Republic of Kosovo|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|South Ossetia}} — To enter South Ossetia, visitors must have a multiple-entry visa for [[Russia]] and register their stay with the Migration Service of the Ministry of Internal Affairs within 3 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.mfa-rso.su/taxonomy/term/13 | title=Порядок въезда на территорию Республики Южная Осетия для иностранных граждан}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://mfa.rsogov.org/node/1398 | title=Порядок въезда на территорию Республики Южная Осетия для иностранных граждан}}</ref>
*{{flag|Transnistria}} — Visa free. Registration required after 24h.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.luxlana.net/Transdniestr.html |title=Transnistria useful information, warnings, visas, border crossings, budget accommodation |access-date=4 August 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131022114723/http://www.luxlana.net/Transdniestr.html |archive-date=22 October 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://transnistria-tour.com/en/rules-and-tipps|title=Rules and recommendations - Transnistria tour|website=transnistria-tour.com|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref>

;Oceania
*{{flag|American Samoa}} — Electronic authorization for 30 days.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://legalaffairs.as.gov/usvisa30day | title=US Visa / Waiver 30-Day Visitor Permit}}</ref>
*{{flagicon|Australia}} [[Ashmore and Cartier Islands]] — special authorisation required.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.environment.gov.au/coasts/mpa/ashmore/activities.html |title=Ashmore Reef National Nature Reserve and Cartier Island Marine Reserve - Activities Allowed |access-date=4 August 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121031132558/http://environment.gov.au/coasts/mpa/ashmore/activities.html |archive-date=31 October 2012 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flagicon|France}} [[Clipperton Island]] — Special permit required.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.clipperton.fr/incagen.html?geopolitique.htm~main|title=Clipperton - Ile de La Passion|first=Bruno|last=Quintero|website=www.clipperton.fr|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref>
*{{flag|Cook Islands}} — Visa free access for 31 days.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.cook-islands.gov.ck/faq.php |title=Cook Islands Government Online |access-date=15 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131115035856/http://www.cook-islands.gov.ck/faq.php |archive-date=15 November 2013 }}</ref>
*{{flag|Guam}} — Visa not required.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=CA|destination=GU|accessdate=26 November 2013}}</ref> 
*{{flag|Niue}} — Visa on arrival valid for 30 days is issued free of charge.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.niueisland.com/getting-niue |title=Getting to Niue &#124; Niue |access-date=1 August 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140824231422/http://www.niueisland.com/getting-niue |archive-date=24 August 2014 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flag|Northern Mariana Islands}} — Visa not required.<ref>{{Timatic|nationality=CA|destination=MP}}</ref>
*{{flag|Pitcairn Islands}} — 14 days visa free and landing fee [[USD]] 35 or tax of USD 5 if not going ashore.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.visitpitcairn.pn/visitpitcairn/visaslegalinfo/touristinfo/index.html |title=Tourist Information &#124; Visas & Legal Info &#124; Pitcairn Island Tourism |access-date=25 September 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131018001850/http://www.visitpitcairn.pn/visitpitcairn/visaslegalinfo/touristinfo/index.html |archive-date=18 October 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.government.pn/visaInfo.php|title=Pitcairn Islands|first=Bill|last=Haigh|website=www.government.pn|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-date=21 October 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171021104351/http://www.government.pn/visaInfo.php|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.government.pn/immigration%20ordinance.pdf |title=Data |website=www.government.pn |access-date=17 November 2013 |archive-date=6 November 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211106205311/http://www.government.pn/immigration%20ordinance.pdf |url-status=dead }}</ref>
*{{flagicon|United States}} [[United States Minor Outlying Islands]] — special permits required for [[Baker Island]], [[Howland Island]], [[Jarvis Island]], [[Johnston Atoll]], [[Kingman Reef]], [[Midway Atoll]], [[Palmyra Atoll]] and [[Wake Island]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/bakerisland/visit.html |title=Visiting - Baker Island National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=16 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017211743/http://www.fws.gov/bakerisland/visit.html |archive-date=17 October 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/howlandisland/visit.html |title=Visiting Howland National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=16 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017212340/http://www.fws.gov/howlandisland/visit.html |archive-date=17 October 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/jarvisisland/|title=Redirect Page|website=www.fws.gov|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-date=4 September 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140904070329/http://www.fws.gov/jarvisisland/|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/johnstonisland/visit.html |title=Visiting Johnston Atoll National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=16 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130607120346/http://www.fws.gov/johnstonisland/visit.html |archive-date=7 June 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/kingmanreef/visit.html |title=Visiting Kingman Reef National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=16 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131017212056/http://www.fws.gov/kingmanreef/visit.html |archive-date=17 October 2013 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/midway/visit.html |title=Visiting Midway Atoll National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=28 January 2014 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140128062001/http://www.fws.gov/midway/visit.html |archive-date=28 January 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fws.gov/palmyraatoll/visit.html |title=Visiting - Palmyra National Wildlife Refuge |access-date=16 November 2013 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130522074332/http://www.fws.gov/palmyraatoll/visit.html |archive-date=22 May 2013 }}</ref>

;South America
* [[File:Bandera Provincia Galápagos.svg|border|22x20px]] [[Galapagos Province|Galápagos]] — 60 days; Visitors must pre-register to receive a 20 USD Transit Control Card (TCT).<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.gobiernogalapagos.gob.ec/para-ingresar-a-la-provincia-de-galapagos/ | title=Para ingresar a la provincia de Galapagos}}</ref>

;South Atlantic and Antarctica
*{{flag|Falkland Islands}} — A visitor permit is normally issued as a stamp in the passport on arrival, The maximum validity period is 1 month.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.gov.fk/customs/visitor-permit/ | title=Visitor Permit}}</ref>
*{{flag|South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands}} — Pre-arrival permit from the commissioner required (72 hours/1 month for 110/160 [[pound sterling|pounds sterling]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fco.gov.uk/en/travel-and-living-abroad/travel-advice-by-country/south-america/south-georgia-south-sandwich#entryRequirements|title=South Georgia and South Sandwich Islands (British Overseas Territory) travel advice - GOV.UK|website=www.fco.gov.uk|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.sgisland.gs/index.php/(v)Information_for_Visitors_to_South_Georgia?useskin=vis |title=Information for Visitors to South Georgia - South Georgia Website |access-date=9 May 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080412170649/http://www.sgisland.gs/index.php/(v)Information_for_Visitors_to_South_Georgia?useskin=vis |archive-date=12 April 2008 |url-status=dead }}</ref>
* [[Antarctica]] and adjacent islands — Special permits required for {{flag|Bouvet Island}}, {{flag|British Antarctic Territory}}, {{flag|French Southern and Antarctic Lands}}, {{flag|Argentine Antarctica}}, {{flagicon|Australia}} [[Australian Antarctic Territory]], {{flagicon|Antártica Chilena Province}} [[Chilean Antarctic Territory]], {{flagicon|Australia}} [[Heard Island and McDonald Islands]], {{flagicon|Norway}} [[Peter I Island]], {{flagicon|Norway}} [[Queen Maud Land]], {{flagicon|New Zealand}} [[Ross Dependency]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.antarctica.ac.uk/about_antarctica/tourism/index.php|title=Antarctic tourism - British Antarctic Survey|website=www.antarctica.ac.uk|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mdulich.com/p/british-antarctic-territory.html |title=British Antarctic Territory ~ MDuLich |website=www.mdulich.com |access-date=12 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170810212141/http://www.mdulich.com/p/british-antarctic-territory.html |archive-date=10 August 2017 |url-status=usurped}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://britishantarcticterritory.fco.gov.uk/en/tourism/|title=British Antarctic Territory - GOV.UK|website=britishantarcticterritory.fco.gov.uk|access-date=29 June 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.taaf.fr/Acces-a-l-Antarctique|title=Accès à l'Antarctique|website=www.taaf.fr|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180501210951/http://www.taaf.fr/Acces-a-l-Antarctique|archive-date=1 May 2018|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.taaf.fr/Acces-aux-iles-australes|title=Accès aux Terres australes françaises|website=www.taaf.fr|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140502032950/http://www.taaf.fr/Acces-aux-iles-australes|archive-date=2 May 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.taaf.fr/Acces-aux-iles-Eparses|title=Accès aux îles Eparses|website=www.taaf.fr|access-date=29 June 2017|archive-url=https://w