==Visa requirements amendment log==
Visa requirements for Canadian citizens were lifted by [[Austria]] in 1956,<ref name="hu-berlin.de">{{cite web | url=https://www.sowi.hu-berlin.de/en/lehrbereiche-en/makro-en/forschung-en/projekte-en/list-of-countries-without-visa-requirements.pdf | title=Data |website=www.sowi.hu-berlin.de}}</ref> [[Finland]] in 1958,<ref name="hu-berlin.de"/> [[Japan]] (20 September 1964),<ref>{{cite web|title=一般旅券査証及び査証料の相互免除に関する日本国政府とカナダ政府との間の交換公文|url=http://www.mofa.go.jp/mofaj/gaiko/treaty/pdfs/A-S39-159.pdf|publisher=Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Japan|access-date=14 February 2018|date=5 September 1964}}</ref> [[Micronesia]] (18 December 1980),<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.fsmcongress.fm/pdf%20documents/1st%20Congress%20of%20the%20FSM/PL%201-130.pdf |title=Immigration Act of Federated States of Micronesia |publisher=The Congress of the Federated States of Micronesia |date=18 December 1980 |access-date=24 February 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141007000014/http://www.fsmcongress.fm/pdf%20documents/1st%20Congress%20of%20the%20FSM/PL%201-130.pdf |archive-date=7 October 2014 |url-status=dead  }}</ref> [[Taiwan]] (1 January 1994),<ref>{{cite web|title=Foreign Relations Yearbook 1997|url=http://mofa.gov.tw:80/chap4.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/19980115051450/http://mofa.gov.tw/chap4.html|archive-date=15 January 1998|publisher=Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Republic of China (Taiwan)|access-date=16 February 2018|language=zh|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Ukraine]] (1 August 2005),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://search.ligazakon.ua/l_doc2.nsf/link1/U1134_05.html|title=Указ Президента №1134/2005 от 26.07.2005, Про встановлення безвізового режиму для громадян Канади|website=search.ligazakon.ua}}</ref> [[Kyrgyzstan]] (27 July 2012),<ref>[http://cbd.minjust.gov.kg/act/view/ru-ru/203721?cl=ru-ru Resolution of the Government of Kyrgyzstanc Republic on 21 July 2012 No. 121] (in Russian)</ref> [[Mongolia]] (1 January 2014), [[Kazakhstan]] (1 January 2017), [[Argentina]] (1 January 2018),<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.balglobal.com/bal-news/argentina-to-waive-visa-reciprocity-fee-for-canadians/|title=Argentina to waive visa reciprocity fee for Canadians - B A L - Berry Appleman & Leiden LLP|newspaper=B a L &#124; Berry Appleman & Leiden LLP}}</ref> [[Armenia]] (10 July 2018),<ref name="auto1">{{cite web|url=https://armenpress.am/eng/news/939112|title=Armenian government plans to introduce visa waiver for Albania, Lebanon, Turkmenistan and Canada|website=Armenpress.am|date=27 June 2018 |access-date=8 July 2018}}</ref><ref name="auto2">{{cite web|url=https://artsakhpress.am/eng/news/88950/armenian-government-plans-to-introduce-visa-waiver-for-albania-lebanon-turkmenistan-and-canada.html|title=Armenian government plans to introduce visa waiver for Albania, Lebanon, Turkmenistan and Canada|website=Artsakhpress.am|access-date=8 July 2018}}</ref><ref name="auto3">{{cite web|url=http://www.beirutbizreport.com/story-z12265056|title=Armenian government plans to introduce visa waiver for Albania, Lebanon, Turkmenistan and Canada |website=Beirutbizreport.com|access-date=8 July 2018}}</ref><ref name="auto4">{{cite web|url=http://arminfo.info/full_news.php?id=32922&lang=3|title=Armenia is going to liberalize the visa regime for the citizens of Canada, Lebanon, Turkmenistan and Albania|website=Arminfo.info|access-date=8 July 2018}}</ref> [[Brazil]] (17 June 2019).<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.cnn.com/travel/article/brazil-lifts-visa-requirement/index.html | title=Tourists from the US, Canada, Japan and Australia can now travel to Brazil visa-free | website=[[CNN]]}}</ref>  and [[Turkey]] (1 January 2024)<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gillett |first=Katy |title=Travel Unpacked: Visa-free travel to Turkey and Etihad launches new India flights |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/travel/2024/01/01/travel-news-round-up/?outputType=amp |access-date=2025-04-05 |website=The National |language=en}}</ref>

Canadian citizens were made eligible for eVisas by [[India]] (1 May 2015),<ref>[http://pib.nic.in/newsite/PrintRelease.aspx?relid=120017 Extension of e-Tourist Visa scheme to 31 more countries], [[Press Information Bureau]], [[Government of India]], 29 April 2015.</ref> [[Brazil]] (25 January 2018, visa free from 17 June 2019 to 10 April 2025),<ref>{{cite news | title=Brazil offers e-visa to Americans in bid to increase tourism | url=http://www.chicagotribune.com/lifestyles/travel/ct-brazil-american-e-visa-20180125-story.html | access-date=24 February 2018 | publisher=Chicago Tribune}}</ref> [[Angola]] (30 March 2018).,<ref>{{cite news | title=Migration service to speed up visa exemption procedure | url=http://www.angop.ao/angola/en_us/noticias/politica/2018/2/13/Migration-service-speed-visa-exemption-procedure,1427fe4a-496a-4e90-9d2f-612f7718cdf9.html | work=ANGOP | language=EN-US}}</ref> [[Namibia]] (1 April 2025)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Important update on visa requirements for international visitors |url=https://visitnamibia.com.na/2024/07/important-update-on-visa-requirements-for-international-visitors/ |access-date=2025-10-19 |language=en-US}}</ref> and [[Brazil]] (10 April 2025)<ref>{{Cite web |title=Visa Requirement Reinstated for Nationals of Australia, Canada and the United States |url=https://www.fragomen.com/insights/brazil-visa-requirement-reinstated-for-nationals-of-australia-canada-and-the-united-states.html |access-date=2025-10-19 |website=Fragomen - Immigration attorneys, solicitors, and consultants worldwide - Visa Requirement Reinstated for Nationals of Australia, Canada and the United States |language=en}}</ref>

